Here is a simple way to do it in MATLAB using the
surf function. First, generate a grid of points $(x,z)$ in $(0,1)^2$ (you can adjust the range according to your needs). Then compute $y=\sqrt{xz}$ and $y=-\sqrt{xz}$ for each point. Finally, plot the surface using these points.

```matlab
[X,Z] = meshgrid(0:0.1:1);
Y1 = sqrt(X .* Z);
Y2 = -sqrt(X .* Z);

figure;
surf(X, Y1, Z, 'FaceColor', 'blue', 'FaceAlpha', 0.5);
hold on;
surf(X, Y2, Z, 'FaceColor', 'red', 'FaceAlpha', 0.5);
hold off;
title('Cone of Positive Definite Matrices');
xlabel('x');
ylabel('z');
zlabel('y');
```

